# Rank 1565 / CVE-2024-32970: Phlex's javascript:-URL guard normalised
# href values by stripping only tabs, spaces and newlines, so a scheme
# carrying other control characters bypassed the check and executed
# script through the rendered attribute (XSS, CWE-79). The attribute
# writer __attributes__ in lib/phlex/sgml.rb did `next if lower_name ==
# "href" && v.to_s.downcase.tr("\t \n", "").start_with?("javascript:")`
# -- browsers strip the full control-character set when parsing URLs,
# so "jav\x01ascript:" and scheme spellings with embedded controls
# survive the tr and are emitted as href values. Fix da8f94342a (its
# lib/phlex/sgml.rb hunk is the security change, bundled with 6613
# lines of XSS fixtures and browser tests): the normalisation becomes
# `v.to_s.downcase.tr("^a-z:", "").start_with?("javascript:")` -- only
# lowercase letters and the colon survive, so no control character can
# hide inside the scheme -- and the unsafe attribute-name check
# normalises with tr("^a-z-", "").
#
# ## What fires, both revisions
#
# Three --cache off runs per revision over lib/ and over the full tree
# report 3 findings at or above high each, identically on the
# vulnerable parent 2f40e77 and the fix: VYQL-INJ-004 on phlex/kit.rb
# const_added (twice) and on SGML.render's renderable parameter. The
# full JSON view holds 3 rows at the parent and 5 at the fix -- the two
# extra are VYQL-RES-001 on browser_tests.rb, a file the fix commit
# itself adds. Zero review flags, and nothing at all on __attributes__
# at either revision: the attribute values reach the buffer through
# `buffer <<` and no HtmlRender sink labels that write, so the guard
# line is the only place the two revisions differ and nothing analyses
# it.
#
# ## Why no binding converts it
#
# A probe binding on the callExpr route can see the strip-set literal:
# `callee.method == "tr" and args.any.literal contains " "` labels the
# weak form (1 on the vulnerable shape, 0 on the fixed shape), because
# the delete-list "\t \n" carries a space and the keep-list "^a-z:"
# does not. That discrimination is the spelling, not the strength:
# `args.any.literal startsWith "^"` -- the keep-list marker, String#tr's
# documented negation -- is rejected by scanner IR lowering ("operator
# not implemented"), and the anchor that would tie the tr to the scheme
# check is unavailable on the same route (node.context.call and
# node.context.scopeCall both "not implemented in scanner IR lowering"
# there), while the presenceNode route that can see the start_with?
# call cannot read the tr argument -- anchor and argument live on
# disjoint routes. Measured collateral of the unanchored form: an
# exhaustive enumeration of `.tr(` with a space in the first string
# argument across every clone under /tmp/cve-work finds 10 sites in 10
# files, of which 2 are this shape (sgml.rb:385 and its repro); the
# other 8 are ordinary string munging -- camelize/underscore name
# folding, a query-string space encoding, and a template text strip
# `tr("\t\r\n\f \"'§;", '')` -- and a genuinely complete delete-set
# (tr("\x00-\x20", "")) carries a space too and would take the label:
# the discriminator fires on enforcing variants, which is the
# fix-layout-keying rejection shape. What would decide the pair is
# normalisation-strength vocabulary, a character-class set comparison
# against the characters the browser URL parser ignores -- two
# vocabularies, unavailable at every layer today. Same
# present-but-incomplete family as ranks 1551, 1522 and 1564. No
# definition change shipped; no pool correction; no ENGINE-GAPS.md
# entry (vocabulary, not a localised construct).
#
# Spec cve_rank1565 records the weak tr form and the strict
# normalisation on the real __attributes__, both asserting reject
# VYQL-INJ-004: when normalisation-strength vocabulary lands, the
# weak-tr form must flip to expect.

test "rank1565: the href scheme check strips three characters only"
  lang ruby
  file lib/phlex/sgml.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  module Phlex
    module SGML
      def __attributes__(attributes, buffer = +"")
        attributes.each do |k, v|
          next unless v

          name = case k
            when String then k
            when Symbol then k.name.tr("_", "-")
            else raise ArgumentError, "Attribute keys should be Strings or Symbols."
          end

          lower_name = name.downcase
          next if lower_name == "href" && v.to_s.downcase.tr("\t \n", "").start_with?("javascript:")

          if HTML::EVENT_ATTRIBUTES.include?(lower_name) || name.match?(/[<>&"']/)
            raise ArgumentError, "Unsafe attribute name detected: #{k}."
          end

          buffer << " " << name << '="' << v.gsub('"', "&quot;") << '"'
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1565: the fixed revision keeps only letters and the colon"
  lang ruby
  file lib/phlex/sgml.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  module Phlex
    module SGML
      def __attributes__(attributes, buffer = +"")
        attributes.each do |k, v|
          next unless v

          name = case k
            when String then k
            when Symbol then k.name.tr("_", "-")
            else raise ArgumentError, "Attribute keys should be Strings or Symbols."
          end

          lower_name = name.downcase
          next if lower_name == "href" && v.to_s.downcase.tr("^a-z:", "").start_with?("javascript:")

          if HTML::EVENT_ATTRIBUTES.include?(lower_name.tr("^a-z-", "")) || name.match?(/[<>&"']/)
            raise ArgumentError, "Unsafe attribute name detected: #{k}."
          end

          buffer << " " << name << '="' << v.gsub('"', "&quot;") << '"'
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```
